<title>MEXICO: Grupo Elektra buys 66.6 pct of Hecali.</title>
<headline>Grupo Elektra buys 66.6 pct of Hecali.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican consumer electronics retailer Grupo Elektra said on Thursday it had exercised its option to buy a 66.6 percent stake in Mexican clothing firm Hecali for 40.8 million pesos.</p>
<p>Of the remaining shares, it said the Saba family bought 18.9 percent, Hecali management kept 9.5 percent and five percent would be distributed via an employee stock option plan.</p>
<p>Hecali, that sells basic clothing to poor Mexicans, has 55 stores in 25 states and employs 607 people. Elektra estimated that the clothing market in Mexico was worth about $5 billion a year.</p>
<p>-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560</p>
